  "note": "OCR damage, recorded as printed. Line 3 right column prints 'ecretary: Deb Arr' and line 4 right column prints \"'ecretary: Katie Berr\"; the high-school pages of the same report (page 132, lines 5-6) print the same two people as 'Secretary Debra Aro' and 'Secretary Katie Berry', which is the likely reading. Line 19 left column prints 'oth Grade:' and is almost certainly '6th Grade:' -- the entries below it carry '6th Grade:' in grade_or_dept per rule 7, and role_raw is untouched. Line 5 left column prints 'Dean of Students: Karma' and the surname 'Tousignant' wraps onto line 6; the two are joined into the line-5 entry. Line 6 also carries the right-column heading 'Specials', so line 6 is filed under headings rather than ignored. Line 42 prints five cafeteria names slash-separated and wrapping onto line 43 ('...Carol' / 'Hamilton/...'); all five are recorded on line 42 and line 43 is the continuation, ignored. Right-column entries on lines 2-4 have grade_or_dept '' because no heading stands above them in that column. Parentheses that enclose a whole role, e.g. 'Nicole Therrien (PE)', are stripped in role_raw; nothing else is normalised."
